        type: "p",
        text: "Another ingredient quietly making its way into contemporary kitchens is black garlic. Its sweet, balsamic-like character, soft texture, and intense umami make it exceptionally versatile. It can be added to sauces, vinaigrettes, purées, marinades, and breads too. For an Indian chef, black garlic can work beautifully with tamarind, *kokum*, roasted aubergine, mushrooms – even a rich dal. A black-garlic naan with smoked butter, let’s say, could be an enticing link between global technique and Indian comfort.",
