        type: "p",
        text: "The future of international cuisine in India, therefore, may be less about authenticity vs. fusion, and more about interpretation. **For, India has always made its own the influences it absorbed from outside – from Persia and Central Asia to Portugal, from Britain to Southeast Asia and beyond**. Today’s global food trends are simply another chapter in that ongoing culinary conversation. And the most exciting dish of tomorrow may not be Korean, Nordic, Japanese, Peruvian, or Indian. It may be unmistakably universal and unquestionably Indian at the same time",
