        text: "An additional factor behind this shift is the ubiquity of digital life. High-definition cameras, video meetings, and social media have made people more aware of how they appear on screen—sometimes referred to as the ‘Zoom effect’. Most men prefer procedures that help them look fresher and more rested, rather than noticeably altered. Dr. Rinky Kapoor, Co-Founder and Director, The Esthetic Clinics, explains, “The biggest shift in male aesthetics is the growing preference for non-surgical procedures that improve skin quality and slow visible ageing without requiring long recovery periods. Botox, hyaluronic acid fillers, laser resurfacing, skin-tightening treatments, and hair-restoration treatments like QR678®, are currently among the most requested procedures in clinics.”",
